{
  "title": "What am I running?",
  "summary": "Read /etc/os-release, uname, lsb_release and hostnamectl, and work out the family from ID and ID_LIKE.",
  "minutes": 12,
  "kind": "lesson",
  "steps": [
    {
      "type": "learn",
      "title": "/etc/os-release",
      "body": [
        "Every modern distro (systemd or not) ships `/etc/os-release`: shell-style `KEY=value` lines.",
        "",
        "```text",
        "$ cat /etc/os-release",
        "PRETTY_NAME=\"Ubuntu 24.04.1 LTS\"",
        "NAME=\"Ubuntu\"",
        "VERSION_ID=\"24.04\"",
        "VERSION=\"24.04.1 LTS (Noble Numbat)\"",
        "VERSION_CODENAME=noble",
        "ID=ubuntu",
        "ID_LIKE=debian",
        "HOME_URL=\"https://www.ubuntu.com/\"",
        "```",
        "",
        "- `ID` is the distro, lowercase. `ID_LIKE` lists the distros it is **compatible with**, closest first (Rocky: `ID_LIKE=\"rhel centos fedora\"`).",
        "- Values may be quoted with `\"` or `'`, or bare.",
        "- Scripts use it like this: `. /etc/os-release; echo \"$ID $VERSION_ID\"`."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "match",
      "prompt": "Match the field to its value on Rocky Linux 9.4.",
      "pairs": [
        [
          "`ID`",
          "`rocky`"
        ],
        [
          "`ID_LIKE`",
          "`rhel centos fedora`"
        ],
        [
          "`VERSION_ID`",
          "`9.4`"
        ],
        [
          "`PRETTY_NAME`",
          "`Rocky Linux 9.4 (Blue Onyx)`"
        ],
        [
          "`PLATFORM_ID`",
          "`platform:el9`"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "learn",
      "title": "The other commands",
      "body": [
        "```text",
        "uname -r          6.8.0-45-generic       kernel release",
        "uname -m          x86_64 / aarch64       CPU architecture",
        "hostnamectl       Operating System: Ubuntu 24.04.1 LTS, Kernel: ..., Architecture: ...",
        "                  (systemd only; also shows virtualization: kvm, wsl, docker...)",
        "lsb_release -a    Distributor ID / Description / Release / Codename",
        "                  (needs the lsb-release package; often missing in containers)",
        "cat /etc/debian_version   /etc/redhat-release   /etc/alpine-release   older per-family files",
        "```",
        "",
        "In a container, `uname -r` shows the **host's** kernel (containers share it), while `/etc/os-release` shows the image's distro. Ask both questions separately."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "mcq",
      "prompt": "Inside an `alpine:3.20` container on an Ubuntu host, `uname -r` prints `6.8.0-45-generic`. Why?",
      "options": [
        "Containers share the host kernel; only the userland comes from the image",
        "Alpine uses Ubuntu's kernel",
        "The image is mislabelled",
        "uname reads /etc/os-release"
      ],
      "answer": 0,
      "explain": "That is the core difference between a container and a VM."
    },
    {
      "type": "sort",
      "prompt": "Which command answers the question?",
      "buckets": [
        "`uname`",
        "`/etc/os-release`"
      ],
      "items": [
        [
          "what kernel version?",
          0
        ],
        [
          "which distro and release?",
          1
        ],
        [
          "arm64 or x86_64?",
          0
        ],
        [
          "what is the codename?",
          1
        ],
        [
          "in a container: what image?",
          1
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "blanks",
      "prompt": "Print the distro ID and version in a shell script.",
      "code": [
        ". __1__",
        "echo \"$__2__ $__3__\""
      ],
      "blanks": [
        "/etc/os-release",
        "ID",
        "VERSION_ID"
      ],
      "bank": [
        "/etc/hostname",
        "NAME_ID",
        "VERSION_LIKE"
      ],
      "explain": "Sourcing the file turns each line into a shell variable."
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "mode": "write",
      "title": "Parse os-release",
      "prompt": [
        "Write `Dictionary<string, string> ParseOsRelease(string text)`:",
        "",
        "- one `KEY=value` per line; skip blank lines and lines starting with `#`, and lines with no `=`.",
        "- strip one pair of matching surrounding quotes (`\"...\"` or `'...'`) from the value.",
        "- the value is everything after the **first** `=` (values may contain `=`).",
        "- trim whitespace around each line. Later duplicates win."
      ],
      "starter": [
        "Dictionary<string, string> ParseOsRelease(string text)",
        "{",
        "    return new Dictionary<string, string>();",
        "}"
      ],
      "solution": [
        "Dictionary<string, string> ParseOsRelease(string text)",
        "{",
        "    var result = new Dictionary<string, string>();",
        "    foreach (var raw in text.Split('\\n'))",
        "    {",
        "        var line = raw.Trim();",
        "        if (line.Length == 0 || line.StartsWith(\"#\")) continue;",
        "        int eq = line.IndexOf('=');",
        "        if (eq <= 0) continue;",
        "        var key = line.Substring(0, eq);",
        "        var value = line.Substring(eq + 1);",
        "        if (value.Length >= 2 && (value[0] == '\"' || value[0] == '\\'') && value[^1] == value[0])",
        "            value = value.Substring(1, value.Length - 2);",
        "        result[key] = value;",
        "    }",
        "    return result;",
        "}"
      ],
      "hints": [
        "Split on `'\\n'`, `Trim()` each line, and use `IndexOf('=')`.",
        "Only strip quotes when the first and last characters are the same quote."
      ],
      "template": [
        "{{CODE}}",
        "var dojoOs = ParseOsRelease(\"PRETTY_NAME=\\\"Ubuntu 24.04.1 LTS\\\"\\nNAME=\\\"Ubuntu\\\"\\nVERSION_ID=\\\"24.04\\\"\\nID=ubuntu\\nID_LIKE=debian\\n# comment\\n\\nBUG_URL='https://bugs.launchpad.net/?a=b'\\n\");",
        "Dojo.Eq(\"PRETTY_NAME unquoted\", \"Ubuntu 24.04.1 LTS\", dojoOs[\"PRETTY_NAME\"]);",
        "Dojo.Eq(\"bare value\", \"ubuntu\", dojoOs[\"ID\"]);",
        "Dojo.Eq(\"VERSION_ID\", \"24.04\", dojoOs[\"VERSION_ID\"]);",
        "Dojo.Eq(\"single quotes and = in value\", \"https://bugs.launchpad.net/?a=b\", dojoOs[\"BUG_URL\"]);",
        "Dojo.Eq(\"comment and blank skipped\", 6, dojoOs.Count);",
        "Dojo.Eq(\"mismatched quotes kept\", \"\\\"oops\", ParseOsRelease(\"X=\\\"oops\")[\"X\"]);"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "mode": "write",
      "title": "Which family?",
      "prompt": [
        "Write `string Family(Dictionary<string, string> os)` returning `\"debian\"`, `\"rhel\"`, `\"suse\"`, `\"arch\"`, `\"alpine\"` or `\"unknown\"`. Look at `ID` first, then each word of `ID_LIKE` in order (case-insensitive), and return the first that is recognised:",
        "",
        "- `debian`, `ubuntu` → debian",
        "- `rhel`, `fedora`, `centos`, `amzn` → rhel",
        "- `suse`, `sles`, or anything starting with `opensuse` → suse",
        "- `arch` → arch; `alpine` → alpine",
        "",
        "Linux Mint has `ID=linuxmint` and `ID_LIKE=\"ubuntu debian\"`, so it is debian. Write your `ParseOsRelease` too, or copy it from the previous step: the tests call both."
      ],
      "starter": [
        "Dictionary<string, string> ParseOsRelease(string text)",
        "{",
        "    var result = new Dictionary<string, string>();",
        "    foreach (var raw in text.Split('\\n'))",
        "    {",
        "        var line = raw.Trim();",
        "        if (line.Length == 0 || line.StartsWith(\"#\")) continue;",
        "        int eq = line.IndexOf('=');",
        "        if (eq <= 0) continue;",
        "        var key = line.Substring(0, eq);",
        "        var value = line.Substring(eq + 1);",
        "        if (value.Length >= 2 && (value[0] == '\"' || value[0] == '\\'') && value[^1] == value[0])",
        "            value = value.Substring(1, value.Length - 2);",
        "        result[key] = value;",
        "    }",
        "    return result;",
        "}",
        "",
        "string Family(Dictionary<string, string> os)",
        "{",
        "    return \"unknown\";",
        "}"
      ],
      "solution": [
        "Dictionary<string, string> ParseOsRelease(string text)",
        "{",
        "    var result = new Dictionary<string, string>();",
        "    foreach (var raw in text.Split('\\n'))",
        "    {",
        "        var line = raw.Trim();",
        "        if (line.Length == 0 || line.StartsWith(\"#\")) continue;",
        "        int eq = line.IndexOf('=');",
        "        if (eq <= 0) continue;",
        "        var key = line.Substring(0, eq);",
        "        var value = line.Substring(eq + 1);",
        "        if (value.Length >= 2 && (value[0] == '\"' || value[0] == '\\'') && value[^1] == value[0])",
        "            value = value.Substring(1, value.Length - 2);",
        "        result[key] = value;",
        "    }",
        "    return result;",
        "}",
        "",
        "string Family(Dictionary<string, string> os)",
        "{",
        "    var ids = new List<string>();",
        "    if (os.TryGetValue(\"ID\", out var id)) ids.Add(id.ToLowerInvariant());",
        "    if (os.TryGetValue(\"ID_LIKE\", out var like)) ids.AddRange(like.ToLowerInvariant().Split(' ', StringSplitOptions.RemoveEmptyEntries));",
        "    foreach (var x in ids)",
        "    {",
        "        if (x == \"debian\" || x == \"ubuntu\") return \"debian\";",
        "        if (x == \"rhel\" || x == \"fedora\" || x == \"centos\" || x == \"amzn\") return \"rhel\";",
        "        if (x == \"suse\" || x.StartsWith(\"opensuse\") || x == \"sles\") return \"suse\";",
        "        if (x == \"arch\") return \"arch\";",
        "        if (x == \"alpine\") return \"alpine\";",
        "    }",
        "    return \"unknown\";",
        "}"
      ],
      "hints": [
        "Build a list: ID first, then the words of ID_LIKE.",
        "Return as soon as one word is recognised."
      ],
      "template": [
        "{{CODE}}",
        "Dojo.Eq(\"ubuntu\", \"debian\", Family(ParseOsRelease(\"ID=ubuntu\\nID_LIKE=debian\")));",
        "Dojo.Eq(\"mint\", \"debian\", Family(ParseOsRelease(\"ID=linuxmint\\nID_LIKE=\\\"ubuntu debian\\\"\")));",
        "Dojo.Eq(\"rocky\", \"rhel\", Family(ParseOsRelease(\"ID=\\\"rocky\\\"\\nID_LIKE=\\\"rhel centos fedora\\\"\")));",
        "Dojo.Eq(\"amazon linux\", \"rhel\", Family(ParseOsRelease(\"ID=\\\"amzn\\\"\\nID_LIKE=\\\"fedora\\\"\")));",
        "Dojo.Eq(\"tumbleweed\", \"suse\", Family(ParseOsRelease(\"ID=\\\"opensuse-tumbleweed\\\"\\nID_LIKE=\\\"opensuse suse\\\"\")));",
        "Dojo.Eq(\"manjaro\", \"arch\", Family(ParseOsRelease(\"ID=manjaro\\nID_LIKE=arch\")));",
        "Dojo.Eq(\"alpine\", \"alpine\", Family(ParseOsRelease(\"ID=alpine\")));",
        "Dojo.Eq(\"nixos\", \"unknown\", Family(ParseOsRelease(\"ID=nixos\")));",
        "Dojo.Eq(\"upper case\", \"rhel\", Family(new Dictionary<string, string> { [\"ID\"] = \"Fedora\" }));"
      ]
    }
  ]
}